  "assessment_rules": "Evaluation is a weighted average of a global test (40%), continuous assessment tests and assignments (40%), and laboratory work (20%). A minimum of 4 out of 10 points is required for the global test, and 3 out of 10 points for laboratory work. Continuous assessment tests and laboratory work are not recoverable in the second call. For exceptional evaluation, students must attend at least 40% of lab sessions, then take a global written test (40%), a practical laboratory test (20%), and an oral theoretical-practical test (40%), requiring a minimum of 4/10 in the written test, 3/10 in other tests, and 5/10 in the weighted average.",
